 "poem": "XIII. OMNES DE ILLUMINUS in\nThe World and the Soul to die, alas!\nThou hast ne'er been born a man of power;\nHe who hath his soul's steed as to heaven,\nThat thou shouldst be a more sublime thing,\nMight tell thy nature at thy command.\nSuch is the sad pride that grows within us;\nI am not, but thou shalt know it never.\nXIV. So thou must die for this our\nHospitable planet; where our\nDusty priests are in all things swarthy and\nAlluring, and they wear their shawls about",
